{"availability":"available","full":"asadarafat/topoviewer","name":"topoviewer","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"Other","language":"TypeScript","stars":25,"forks":6,"created":"2022-11-19T12:54:27Z","updated":"2026-10-11T13:29:04Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"development","homepage":"https://asadarafat.github.io/topoviewer/","topics":[],"demo":"https://asadarafat.github.io/topoviewer/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T13:33:41.571Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-12T13:33:41.571Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-12T13:33:41.571Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T11:02:39.348Z","stars":25,"forks":6},{"at":"2026-10-12T13:33:41.571Z","stars":25,"forks":6}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Topology as Code for infrastructure, network, and service diagrams.","TopoViewer turns declarative YAML into interactive, validated topology diagrams. It keeps object identity, visual policy, and runtime state separate, so a topology can be reviewed in Git and rendered consistently in docs, products, and operational dashboards.","TopoViewer is not a general whiteboard. Mermaid, Excalidraw, diagrams.net, and PowerPoint remain better for one-off sketches. TopoViewer earns its place when topology identity must survive beyond one drawing."],"features":["reviewable as YAML in pull requests;","validated through schemas and semantic checks;","reusable across docs, React products, and dashboards;","layered so one model can expose physical, logical, service, or transport views;","consistent through selector-based visual policy;"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/asadarafat/topoviewer/blob/development/README.md","fingerprint":"0d9c9fbca8d638affbc398ca9b9c1d2b7de9122f6b1a9158ab41a3bd0821f552","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T11:02:39.485Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T11:02:39.485Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Topology as Code for infrastructure, network, and service diagrams.","sourceUrl